# Line endings normalized to LF in the repo (git still converts them on
# read/write according to the local core.autocrlf) — without this file, on a
# Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true any git operation that touches a
# file (checkout, stash, pull) rewrites it in CRLF, making `prettier --check`
# (default endOfLine: "lf") fail even when the content has not really
# changed. Seen in practice on files just written and already formatted
# correctly.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
